{
  "id": "JER.44",
  "number": "44",
  "bookId": "JER",
  "reference": "Jeremiah 44",
  "verseCount": 30,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "44",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "JER 44"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "44",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews that dwelt in the land of Egypt, at Migdol, at Tahpanhes, at Memphis, and in the land of Pathros, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " of hosts, the God of Israel: You have seen all the evil that I brought upon Jerusalem and upon all the cities of Judah. Behold, this day they are a desolation, and no one dwells in them, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "because of the wickedness which they committed, provoking me to anger, in that they went to burn incense and serve other gods that they knew not, neither they, nor you, nor your fathers. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet I persistently sent to you all my servants the prophets, saying, ‘Oh, do not do this abominable thing that I hate!’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But they did not listen or incline their ear, to turn from their wickedness and burn no incense to other gods. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore my wrath and my anger were poured forth and kindled in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; and they became a waste and a desolation, as at this day. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And now thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " God of hosts, the God of Israel: Why do you commit this great evil against yourselves, to cut off from you man and woman, infant and child, from the midst of Judah, leaving you no remnant? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Why do you provoke me to anger with the works of your hands, burning incense to other gods in the land of Egypt where you have come to live, that you may be cut off and become a curse and a taunt among all the nations of the earth? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Have you forgotten the wickedness of your fathers, the wickedness of the kings of Judah, the wickedness of their",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "44.9",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "his",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " wives, your own wickedness, and the wickedness of your wives, which they committed in the land of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They have not humbled themselves even to this day, nor have they feared, nor walked in my law and my statutes which I set before you and before your fathers.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Therefore thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " of hosts, the God of Israel: Behold, I will set my face against you for evil, to cut off all Judah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will take the remnant of Judah who have set their faces to come to the land of Egypt to live, and they shall all be consumed; in the land of Egypt they shall fall; by the sword and by famine they shall be consumed; from the least to the greatest, they shall die by the sword and by famine; and they shall become an execration, a horror, a curse, and a taunt. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will punish those who dwell in the land of Egypt, as I have punished Jerusalem, with the sword, with famine, and with pestilence, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "so that none of the remnant of Judah who have come to live in the land of Egypt shall escape or survive or return to the land of Judah, to which they desire to return to dwell there; for they shall not return, except some fugitives.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then all the men who knew that their wives had offered incense to other gods, and all the women who stood by, a great assembly, all the people who dwelt in Pathros in the land of Egypt, answered Jeremiah: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“As for the word which you have spoken to us in the name of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", we will not listen to you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But we will do everything that we have vowed, burn incense to the queen of heaven and pour out libations to her, as we did, both we and our fathers, our kings and our princes, in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; for then we had plenty of food, and prospered, and saw no evil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But since we left off burning incense to the queen of heaven and pouring out libations to her, we have lacked everything and have been consumed by the sword and by famine.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the women said,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "44.19",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Compare Syr: Heb lacks",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "And the women said",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " “When we burned incense to the queen of heaven and poured out libations to her, was it without our husbands' approval that we made cakes for her bearing her image and poured out libations to her?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Jeremiah said to all the people, men and women, all the people who had given him this answer: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“As for the incense that you burned in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem, you and your fathers, your kings and your princes, and the people of the land, did not the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " remember it?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "44.21",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Syr: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "them",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Did it not come into his mind? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " could no longer bear your evil doings and the abominations which you committed; therefore your land has become a desolation and a waste and a curse, without inhabitant, as it is this day. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is because you burned incense, and because you sinned against the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and did not obey the voice of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " or walk in his law and in his statutes and in his testimonies, that this evil has befallen you, as at this day.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jeremiah said to all the people and all the women, “Hear the word of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", all you of Judah who are in the land of Egypt, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " of hosts, the God of Israel: You and your wives have declared with your mouths, and have fulfilled it with your hands, saying, ‘We will surely perform our vows that we have made, to burn incense to the queen of heaven and to pour out libations to her.’ Then confirm your vows and perform your vows! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore hear the word of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", all you of Judah who dwell in the land of Egypt: Behold, I have sworn by my great name, says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", that my name shall no more be invoked by the mouth of any man of Judah in all the land of Egypt, saying, ‘As the Lord ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " lives.’ ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Behold, I am watching over them for evil and not for good; all the men of Judah who are in the land of Egypt shall be consumed by the sword and by famine, until there is an end of them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And those who escape the sword shall return from the land of Egypt to the land of Judah, few in number; and all the remnant of Judah, who came to the land of Egypt to live, shall know whose word will stand, mine or theirs. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This shall be the sign to you, says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", that I will punish you in this place, in order that you may know that my words will surely stand against you for evil: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 44:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus says the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", Behold, I will give Pharaoh Hophra king of Egypt into the hand of his enemies and into the hand of those who seek his life, as I gave Zedekiah king of Judah into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, who was his enemy and sought his life.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.44.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.44.30"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
